                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "25940202",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198278912293",
                            "num_reviews": 12,
                            "playtime_forever": 29,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 29,
                            "last_played": 1475989572
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game kind of broke my heart. It looks like it is going to be something special while it is barely a game at all. What you do is try to get along side another airship and your ship auto fires guns. That is the game. You turn and go up and down, nothing more. You can pilot a smaller ship from your larger vessel but the gameplay is the same.  Nothing in the game has collision. You can fly through buildings and other ships. There are some pretty cool looking mechanical birds that fly around and... fly through your ship without any collision. This should definitely not be $10.  I've got tons of judder on my 6700K 1070 rig. It's possible that is a problem on my end though I dont have issues with any other games. This is only the second game I've ever refunded. Maybe I'll check it out again in 6 months if it's still around.",
                        "timestamp_created": 1475990087,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1475990087,
                        "voted_up": false,
                        "votes_up": 31,
                        "votes_funny": 1,
                        "weighted_vote_score": 0.7322049736976624,
                        "comment_count": 3,
                        "steam_purchase": true,
                        "received_for_free": false,
                        "written_during_early_access": true,
                        "developer_response": "Hey Choates. Appreciate the feedback and sincerely take it to heart.\n\nWe tried to extend the gameplay with additional gametypes (Interdiction, VIP Snatch, Escort), but clearly need to focus on the core mechanics.\n\nI hope you revisit the game as additional updates are released!",
